The '''2011 NBA draft''' was held on June 23, 2011, at [[Prudential Center]] in [[Newark, New Jersey]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Report: NBA draft moving to Newark|url=https://www.espn.com/nba/news/story?id=5733121|work=ESPN.com|access-date=October 27, 2010|date=October 27, 2010| archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20101030154621/http://sports.espn.go.com/nba/news/story?id=5733121| archive-date= 30 October 2010 | url-status= live}}</ref> The draft started at 8:00&nbsp;p.m. [[Eastern Time Zone|Eastern Daylight Time]] (23:00 [[Coordinated Universal Time|UTC]]), and was broadcast in the United States on [[ESPN]]. [[Kia Motors]] was the presenting sponsor of the 2011 NBA draft.<ref>{{cite web|title=Kia Motors becomes presenting partner of 2011 NBA Draft|url=https://pr.nba.com/kia-motors-2011-nba-draft/|work=NBA Communications|access-date=June 13, 2011|date=June 13, 2011|archive-date=October 12, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191012121616/https://pr.nba.com/kia-motors-2011-nba-draft/|url-status=live}}</ref> In this [[Draft (sports)|draft]], [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA) teams took turns selecting amateur U.S. [[college basketball]] players and other eligible players, including international players. The [[Cleveland Cavaliers]] had the first pick due to a previous trade they had involving the [[Los Angeles Clippers]], choosing [[point guard]] [[Kyrie Irving]] of [[Duke Blue Devils men's basketball|Duke]]. Of the 60 players drafted, 7 were [[Freshman|freshmen]], 7 were [[sophomore]]s, 14 were [[Junior (education year)|juniors]], 19 were [[Senior (education)|seniors]], 12 were international players without U.S. college basketball experience (including the first-ever [[Qatar]]i-selected player), and 1 was a [[NBA Development League|D-League]] player.

The 2011 NBA draft marked the final time the [[Brooklyn Nets|New Jersey Nets]] made an NBA draft appearance. After the end of the Nets' [[2011–12 New Jersey Nets season|2011–12 season]], the franchise relocated to [[Brooklyn]], [[New York (state)|New York]] and was renamed to the Brooklyn Nets. The Nets made their first draft appearance with the Brooklyn moniker in [[2012 NBA draft|2012]]. Four of the first-round picks, including three of the top four picks, Kyrie Irving, Derrick Williams, Tristan Thompson, and Iman Shumpert, would all eventually become teammates on the Cleveland Cavaliers. The 2011 draft is considered one of the most abundant drafts in NBA history; seven players in the draft would play in at least two All-Star games and six were selected to at least one All-NBA Team, including the final pick of the draft, [[Isaiah Thomas (basketball)|Isaiah Thomas]]. As of 2025, eight players from this draft remained in the NBA during its [[2025–26 NBA season|2025–26 season]]: Irving, [[Jonas Valančiūnas]], [[Bismack Biyombo]], [[Klay Thompson]], [[Kawhi Leonard]], [[Nikola Vučević]], [[Tobias Harris]], and [[Jimmy Butler]].

